#: ../../source/nth-check_README.md:3
msgid "Parses and compiles CSS nth-checks to highly optimized functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/nth-check_README.md:5
msgid "About"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/nth-check_README.md:7
msgid ""
"This module can be used to parse & compile nth-checks, as they are found "
"in CSS 3's `nth-child()` and `nth-last-of-type()`. It can be used to "
"check if a given index matches a given nth-rule, or to generate a "
"sequence of indices matching a given nth-rule."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/nth-check_README.md:9
msgid ""
"`nth-check` focusses on speed, providing optimized functions for "
"different kinds of nth-child formulas, while still following the "
"[spec](http://www.w3.org/TR/css3-selectors/#nth-child-pseudo)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/nth-check_README.md:11
msgid "API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/nth-check_README.md:17
msgid "`nthCheck(formula)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/nth-check_README.md:19
msgid ""
"Parses and compiles a formula to a highly optimized function. Combination"
" of `parse` and `compile`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/nth-check_README.md:21
msgid ""
"If the formula doesn't match any elements, it returns "
"[`boolbase`](https://github.com/fb55/boolbase)'s `falseFunc`. Otherwise, "
"a function accepting an _index_ is returned, which returns whether or not"
" the passed _index_ matches the formula."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/nth-check_README.md:23
msgid ""
"**Note**: The nth-rule starts counting at `1`, the returned function at "
"`0`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/nth-check_README.md:25 ../../source/nth-check_README.md:43
#: ../../source/nth-check_README.md:53
msgid "**Example:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/nth-check_README.md:39
msgid "`parse(formula)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/nth-check_README.md:41
msgid ""
"Parses the expression, throws an `Error` if it fails. Otherwise, returns "
"an array containing the integer step size and the integer offset of the "
"nth rule."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/nth-check_README.md:49
msgid "`compile([a, b])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/nth-check_README.md:51
msgid ""
"Takes an array with two elements (as returned by `.parse`) and returns a "
"highly optimized function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/nth-check_README.md:67
msgid "`generate([a, b])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/nth-check_README.md:69
msgid ""
"Returns a function that produces a monotonously increasing sequence of "
"indices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/nth-check_README.md:71
msgid ""
"If the sequence has an end, the returned function will return `null` "
"after the last index in the sequence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/nth-check_README.md:73 ../../source/nth-check_README.md:100
msgid "**Example:** An always increasing sequence"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/nth-check_README.md:85 ../../source/nth-check_README.md:112
msgid "**Example:** With an end value"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/nth-check_README.md:96
msgid "`sequence(formula)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/nth-check_README.md:98
msgid ""
"Parses and compiles a formula to a generator that produces a sequence of "
"indices. Combination of `parse` and `generate`."
msgstr ""

